{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"f02b1d21-d2b0-4b58-95dd-861600690ee6","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The Intervals.icu OAuth integration issues have been resolved, and the root causes and analysis of the colleague's notes have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-O7FlzT/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **OAuth Init Flow (`401 Unauthorized` fix)**:\n   - Updated the init endpoint in [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-O7FlzT/server.py) to accept `POST /api/intervals/auth/init` and return JSON `{\"authorize_url\": ...}`.\n   - Updated the frontend in [`static/app.js`](file:///tmp/h-O7FlzT/static/app.js) to trigger an authenticated POST fetch request with the athlete's bearer token from `localStorage` and navigate via `window.location.assign(res.authorize_url)` instead of a raw `\u003ca\u003e` navigation.\n\n2. **OAuth Scopes (`Duplicate scope` fix)**:\n   - Modified `SCOPES` in [`config.py`](file:///tmp/h-O7FlzT/config.py) from `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` to `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. In Intervals.icu, `:WRITE` implies `:READ`; specifying both causes an `invalid_request` error.\n\n3. **Perpetual Credentials \u0026 Lazy Revocation (`expired, reconnect` after 1h fix)**:\n   - Removed the artificial 1-hour expiry fallback and the background token refresh loop in [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-O7FlzT/server.py), as Intervals.icu tokens do not expire or issue a `refresh_token`.\n   - Implemented lazy revocation in `intervals_get`: if Intervals.icu returns `401 Unauthorized`, the token is cleared and the status transitions to `expired, reconnect`.\n\n4. **Token Exchange**:\n   - Updated `exchange_code()` in [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-O7FlzT/server.py) to send only `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code` as required by Intervals.icu's token endpoint.\n","duration_seconds":173.974671,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":203078,"output_tokens":9114,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":1302431,"total_tokens":212192}}}
